A||||11||88formula||Lightening the fiero||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||04-22-2001||10:09 PM||||What’s the lightest anyone here has ever gotten there fiero and how did you do it?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-22-2001||10:14 PM||||Remove all the body panels, the seats, the tires, the center console, dash, carpets, rubber weather stripping, engine, gas tank and a few other parts, tou can get the weight down considerably.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||04-22-2001||10:20 PM||||Ex Fiero autocrosser George Ryan had his coupe down to 1900lbs with a Quad 4 , the car was gutted , lexan windows , lightened doors , just about everything done to it you can imagine to get it light<P>the car had a 232hp manapart built motor , impressive package. George got out of fiero's for various reasons , the car is now owned by a gentlemen in Arizona part of "Team python" the one guy has a 4.5ltr caddy motor in his autocross car..also very fast<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||04-23-2001||06:04 PM||||The Doors almost weigh a hundred pounds each. How do you guys go about lightening them?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||04-23-2001||06:06 PM||||Yeah, the doors are a beast.. I have 2 sitting here, but never really bothered to look into them. I ASSUME you could gut them considerably (but what about th safety?? yaya. You make the choice)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||04-23-2001||10:43 PM||||Gm makes an alum. V6 block.<BR>the cost is of course high. ;-)<BR>I'm not sure what mine is down to but I removed the air cond, all of it's brackets<BR>and hoses, pass. seat,spare tire, jack,<BR>cruz-control, light weight racing wheels,<BR>and replaced the drivers seat with a racing<BR>seat. Was going to take out stereo but the Alpine doesn't even weigh two pnds.<BR>Feels much lighter.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000006||PJ||04-23-2001||10:53 PM||||Hey, I took out over 100 lbs. Then I put the roll cage in and I was back where I started from.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||ROB MAC||04-24-2001||11:39 AM||||I put mine on a hoist and hit the frame with an air hammer for a minute or two. Knocked about 30 pounds of rust off.||||reg||1
Z||000008||80's BOY||04-24-2001||12:48 PM||||i cut the top out of mine....the edges are kinda sharp, but it seemed like a good idea at the time <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000009||Will||04-24-2001||03:18 PM||||If you totally reqire the car you could save a few pounds, since all chassis' are wired for all power options available that year.||||reg||1
Z||000010||lou_dias||04-25-2001||10:08 AM||||go with tubular control arms, smaller rims bigger tire<BR>aluminum block...convert to car setup and get aluminum heads too...<BR>remove the steel saftey beams from the doors...<P>If you want to get real fancy, find that company in Canada I think that had designed the prototype 90 chasis with the aluminum sub-frame...  Remeber the HO Quad 4 GT with the aluminum subframe on the GM test track that could out handle and out run the Vette's of the time...tragic really...||||reg||1
Z||000011||lou_dias||04-25-2001||10:16 AM||||...carbon fiber...<BR>...hmm...<BR>aren't entire chasis of the newer Diablos carbon fiber?  Come on, where's the autocad drawings of the engine cradle...do that over in carbon fiber or aluminum and you'd have that 50/50 weight differential...<P>What about the front suspension cross-member...  That's simple enough...  Hell, Ryane (Held) Motorsports designed a brand new one for their slalom sport suspension...how hard is it to make a factory one out of aluminum or CB...<P>Look at the advantages of a lighter car:<BR>better braking<BR>better handling<BR>better acceleration<BR>better fuel ecomony<P>now that's what I call a performance upgrade||||reg||1
